rota lap 4970, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Read foundations/20260826-021731_aether-the-row-that-hears.md. Its instruction is to listen for the claim a page keeps repeating and for the silence where a claim used to be; both fired on one function -- the lock's comment repeating a two-line window over a 50ms poll, and three guards over the lock's scope with none over its protocol.
file rye/src/main.rye build_lock_claim publishes the lock complete by rename; build_lock_stall opens its one window on demand, bounded and off by default
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_build_lock_holder_control.sh 28 legs, two compilers from tracked sources, the elder's fault shown before the repair lifts it
file tools/r/rye_build_lock_holder_witness.rish the five readings asserted by name so none goes silent behind a green tally
file construction/REDS.md the row at %743 after two collisions, with the wrong first repair recorded beside the right one
file construction/archive/REDS-a-reading-of-nothing-rows-519-532.md the fold the pin owed, two rows that each stopped reading their subject
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri rye_build_lock_holder at tier cadence, beside the sibling that reads the same lock's scope
file construction/ITINERARY.md the account, and the compiler-staleness gap named as a proposal rather than taken
obs THE SEND MET TWO LEDGER COLLISIONS IN ONE ROUND, both the shape the derived spine names. I booked %741 off a
fetched next-free; a peer landed %740 and %741 while I worked, so mine became %742; a second rebase found a peer
already published at %742 with a LATER stamp, and because theirs was shared and mine was not, mine shifted again to
%743. The law's confinement held both times: only the unshared row moved, and the stamp never did.
obs AND THE PIN OWED A FOLD, WHICH I TOOK RATHER THAN SHAVING MY OWN ROW FOR A SHARED OVERFLOW. My row was already
1,635 bytes and the pin was 1,541 over; three peer rows had landed on it today. Rows %519 and %532 went to a shelf
whose head says what they teach together -- each an instrument that had quietly stopped reading its subject -- and
the pin reads 60,071 with the spine gapless.
obs I THEN MADE THE VERY ERROR RULE 5 EXISTS FOR. The claim-close follow-up carried real content and did NOT carry
the card's nib forward, so remember_git_nib went stale on the next reading. This commit is the repair the rule
prescribes -- a following work commit that moves the pin -- rather than a force-push or a pin-only commit, both
of which are forbidden.
scope one race found by reading a comment against its code, one ledger fold the pin owed, one protocol repaired, one pen proving it from both sides, one gap named and left
status GREEN on rye_build_lock_holder, tame_style_check and width-check on metal; the cold roster was still running at write time and three of its reds are named in the account, one of them mine
recommend check in (Keaton) -- the compiler-staleness reading wants your word on whether it joins the roster, and the 702 unlocked call sites want a ruling on whether the shell-side lock retires now that the compiler's own holds
